 "text": "**Situation**\n- OEM-A raised FB-ARKA by 40.0% for February; the forecast already shows 36.9% more FB-ARKA demand in six weeks (Lebaran ramp).\n- The 3,500 t group (IMM-04/05, the only machines that fit the ARKA molds) is short by 18.3%; IMM-04 is the bottleneck at 159.4% load and its cycle time is 79.28 s vs 68.0 s ideal (breakdown risk high, alarm in 6.9 days).\n- Resin PP-EPDM-T20 runs out on 2027-02-09 (8 days); the usual vendor is late. Lot LOT-PPT20-0918 shows a gas mark and bubble lift. 3 orders are at risk (penalty exposure Rp190,000,000).\n\n**Actions (priority order)**\n1. Preventive maintenance on IMM-04 (2 h stop) — restores the cycle time and removes the breakdown risk.\n2. Move the FB-ARKA mold to IMM-05 (swap with RB-ARKA, 90 min changeover) — CP-SAT fill rate with maintenance and mold moves: 90.5%.\n3. PO 160,000 kg PP-EPDM-T20 from PT Merapi Resin Indonesia (arrives before the stockout).\n4. Quality hold on resin lot LOT-PPT20-0918.\n5. Revise the ship dates of 3 orders and send the drafted customer notice.\n\n**Plan total (impact_calculator):** Rp3,855,841,000 saved or avoided, 1,889 kg scrap avoided, 7,405 kWh and 6,443 kg CO2e saved per month.\n\n**If nothing is done:** IMM-04 is likely to fail within about a week, molding stops for lack of resin around 2027-02-09, and the 3 late orders cost Rp190,000,000 in penalties.\n\nAll actions are pending your approval in the Action Center.",
